1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:07,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:08,746 --> 00:00:11,483
is taking today off.

3
00:00:11,549 --> 00:00:12,750
Why?

4
00:00:14,853 --> 00:00:15,920
To be honest…

5
00:00:17,255 --> 00:00:21,359
he has a very serious illness
and doesn't have much time left to live.

6
00:00:21,426 --> 00:00:22,560
He was hiding it from us.

7
00:00:24,262 --> 00:00:26,164
What? What the heck?

8
00:00:26,231 --> 00:00:28,800
By illness, do you mean cancer
or something?

9
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:32,203
So we won't get to see Onicchi again?

10
00:00:41,913 --> 00:00:43,781
Wait, everyone, please calm down.

11
00:00:43,848 --> 00:00:45,183
Miss, that can't be true!

12
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:46,584
Please say it isn't true!

13
00:00:47,152 --> 00:00:48,319
It isn't true!

14
00:00:50,355 --> 00:00:51,189
What?

15
00:00:51,256 --> 00:00:54,025
He just has a regular summer cold.

16
00:00:54,726 --> 00:00:56,794
Apparently, he left the AC on all night

17
00:00:56,861 --> 00:00:59,497
and slept with
his stomach exposed like a kid.

18
00:01:01,733 --> 00:01:04,068
Then, why did you lie to us?

19
00:01:04,636 --> 00:01:05,770
I'm sorry.

20
00:01:05,837 --> 00:01:08,606
Mr. Onizuka begged me to do it.

21
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:14,112
He wanted to see everyone's reaction
to know how much he is loved, I think.

22
00:01:14,179 --> 00:01:15,180
What the heck?

23
00:01:15,246 --> 00:01:17,949
Still, isn't this prank
going a bit too far?

24
00:01:18,016 --> 00:01:19,884
I didn't want to do it either!

25
00:01:19,951 --> 00:01:23,054
But, when I refused, he threatened
to reveal my secret to you.

26
00:01:23,121 --> 00:01:24,489
Your secret?

27
00:01:25,056 --> 00:01:26,858
I have no idea what it could be,

28
00:01:26,925 --> 00:01:30,128
but he said it was a super crazy one
that would shock all of you,

29
00:01:30,195 --> 00:01:31,362
so I couldn't refuse.

30
00:01:31,429 --> 00:01:32,697
I don't get it at all!

31
00:01:32,764 --> 00:01:35,767
When all is said and done,
Ms. Kashiwabara,

32
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:38,303
haven't you started
to resemble Mr. Onizuka?

33
00:01:38,870 --> 00:01:39,704
What?

34
00:01:39,771 --> 00:01:42,807
Lately, you've been
pretty influenced by him.

35
00:01:42,874 --> 00:01:46,911
You've been butting into
other people's business, just like him.

36
00:01:46,978 --> 00:01:48,179
Hold on, stop that.

37
00:01:48,246 --> 00:01:51,049
Being a teacher isn't even…

38
00:01:51,115 --> 00:01:52,550
Being a teacher…

39
00:01:53,718 --> 00:01:54,752
What about it?

40
00:01:56,421 --> 00:01:57,255
Nothing.

41
00:01:57,822 --> 00:01:59,724
Let's start homeroom.

42
00:02:00,291 --> 00:02:04,596
Now that summer vacation is over,
some of you may still be taking it easy…

43
00:02:10,101 --> 00:02:12,604
Wow, without that problem teacher around,

44
00:02:12,670 --> 00:02:16,674
the air in the staff room
feels so refreshing.

45
00:02:16,741 --> 00:02:19,244
This is truly how the academy
was meant to be.

46
00:02:19,310 --> 00:02:22,213
If possible, I wish he would
take off forever!

47
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:24,249
Vice Principal, do you have a moment?

48
00:02:24,315 --> 00:02:26,117
Yes, what is it?

49
00:02:26,184 --> 00:02:30,154
But doesn't it feel sad
without Mr. Onizuka around?

50
00:02:30,221 --> 00:02:33,691
I was feeling that too.
Like something is missing.

51
00:02:33,758 --> 00:02:37,095
It's problematic for me
if he doesn't come back soon.

52
00:02:37,662 --> 00:02:41,633
Ms. Kashiwabara, do you also
feel sad without Mr. Onizuka?

53
00:02:41,699 --> 00:02:45,536
No! I just don't want to be
in charge of the class.

54
00:02:48,806 --> 00:02:49,774
What? No way.

55
00:02:50,541 --> 00:02:51,409
Something wrong?

56
00:02:52,477 --> 00:02:53,711
No, nothing really.

57
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:04,989
To my dearest wife, how are you?

58
00:03:05,056 --> 00:03:07,792
On my end, perhaps because
I was working too hard

59
00:03:07,859 --> 00:03:10,895
at my assigned school,
I've caught a summer cold.

60
00:03:10,962 --> 00:03:13,097
I have a high fever
and can't stop coughing.

61
00:03:13,665 --> 00:03:18,403
Oh, but don't worry,
no need to nurse me or anything.

62
00:03:19,037 --> 00:03:22,240
However, if you insist on coming back…

63
00:03:22,307 --> 00:03:23,641
Oh, but I still haven't

64
00:03:23,708 --> 00:03:27,245
come up with an answer
to what a Great Teacher is…

65
00:03:27,312 --> 00:03:31,683
I feel anxious being alone though…

66
00:03:31,749 --> 00:03:34,552
Please, come back home.

67
00:03:40,692 --> 00:03:42,026
TAXI

68
00:04:11,022 --> 00:04:12,657
Huh? What's wrong?

69
00:04:12,724 --> 00:04:14,258
Ms. Kashiwabara.

70
00:04:14,325 --> 00:04:17,495
I was passing nearby,
so I bought you some fruit.

71
00:04:17,562 --> 00:04:19,497
I was worried you weren't eating properly.

72
00:04:20,365 --> 00:04:23,167
Oh, I'm sorry. Thank you very much.

73
00:04:23,234 --> 00:04:24,369
Come in.

74
00:04:24,435 --> 00:04:26,037
Excuse me.

75
00:04:35,446 --> 00:04:36,280
Come in.

76
00:04:36,347 --> 00:04:37,215
Excuse me.

77
00:04:37,281 --> 00:04:39,217
Sorry, it's so messy… Oh, no!

78
00:04:42,053 --> 00:04:43,454
I don't mind.

79
00:04:43,521 --> 00:04:44,422
Okay.

80
00:04:44,489 --> 00:04:47,725
The students were angry, you know.
Because of the lie you told.

81
00:04:48,326 --> 00:04:49,160
I'm sorry.

82
00:04:49,227 --> 00:04:54,298
It's like wanting to know
what people would say at your funeral.

83
00:04:54,365 --> 00:04:55,666
I was super curious.

84
00:04:55,733 --> 00:05:00,538
If you have time to think about that,
I need you to hurry up and get better.

85
00:05:00,605 --> 00:05:02,607
Oh, really?

86
00:05:04,142 --> 00:05:05,176
Well…

87
00:05:05,676 --> 00:05:07,712
This may not be the right time…

88
00:05:09,347 --> 00:05:12,717
-I must tell you something important.
-What? Oh, okay.

89
00:05:12,784 --> 00:05:13,618
What is it?

90
00:05:14,485 --> 00:05:15,753
Mr. Onizuka.

91
00:05:17,488 --> 00:05:19,123
Actually, I…

92
00:05:19,190 --> 00:05:22,260
Ms. Kashiwabara, I have a wife…

93
00:05:22,326 --> 00:05:23,761
Yes, I know that.

94
00:05:23,828 --> 00:05:27,365
Then, you don't need to say anything.
Let's stop here.

95
00:05:27,432 --> 00:05:29,133
No, I can't do that…

96
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:32,103
No, I need to prepare myself too…

97
00:05:32,170 --> 00:05:36,474
I had no idea
that you felt that way about me…

98
00:05:37,708 --> 00:05:39,677
Sorry, are you misunderstanding something?

99
00:05:40,244 --> 00:05:41,045
What?

100
00:05:41,112 --> 00:05:45,917
A while ago, I applied to a company,
and they've now sent me an offer.

101
00:05:45,983 --> 00:05:47,185
So I'm thinking of quitting.

102
00:05:47,251 --> 00:05:49,020
HUMAN RESOURCES

103
00:05:49,086 --> 00:05:50,521
You startled me.

104
00:05:50,588 --> 00:05:55,493
I mean, you were looking at me
with such dreamy eyes…

105
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:58,329
I'm out of contacts, so I can't see!

106
00:05:59,163 --> 00:06:00,131
So that's why…

107
00:06:02,166 --> 00:06:04,836
Wait! Did you just say
you're quitting the school?

108
00:06:04,902 --> 00:06:05,736
Yes.

109
00:06:05,803 --> 00:06:08,473
So, you need to return quickly.

110
00:06:08,539 --> 00:06:10,174
No! You're joking, right?

111
00:06:10,241 --> 00:06:14,545
I told you before,
I never had plans to be a teacher forever.

112
00:06:14,612 --> 00:06:16,681
I'm thinking of resigning
as early as tomorrow.

113
00:06:16,747 --> 00:06:18,449
No, wait a second.

114
00:06:18,516 --> 00:06:22,153
When I asked before, I said
we'd talk about that again later, but…

115
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:23,354
You can't quit.

116
00:06:23,421 --> 00:06:26,424
Out of everyone I know,
you're the most suited to being a teacher.

117
00:06:26,491 --> 00:06:28,159
That's just your assumption.

118
00:06:28,226 --> 00:06:31,462
Besides, the new company
will pay me much better.

119
00:06:31,529 --> 00:06:32,597
Don't be like that.

120
00:06:32,663 --> 00:06:33,898
Take care.

121
00:06:33,965 --> 00:06:35,766
Oh, wait, Ms. Kashiwabara.

122
00:06:43,875 --> 00:06:46,444
AZUSA - SEEMS YOU ALREADY HAVE
A WOMAN TAKING CARE OF YOU, HUH?

123
00:06:48,279 --> 00:06:49,780
No way.

124
00:06:50,348 --> 00:06:52,884
"It's a misunderstanding.
A misunderstanding!"

125
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,488
Sorry.

126
00:08:27,812 --> 00:08:28,879
Good morning.

127
00:08:32,883 --> 00:08:33,718
Good morning.

128
00:08:34,652 --> 00:08:35,753
Good morning.

129
00:08:39,590 --> 00:08:43,561
You know, with Onizuka gone,
it's nice and quiet, isn't it?

130
00:08:44,128 --> 00:08:47,732
Is it? For me, it's too ordinary,
so it's a bit boring.

131
00:08:48,833 --> 00:08:51,535
Hey, I've been wondering for a while.

132
00:08:52,603 --> 00:08:55,139
Do you have a boyfriend?

133
00:08:57,541 --> 00:08:58,476
Why?

134
00:08:59,644 --> 00:09:02,813
If you do, I was wondering
how you found him.

135
00:09:03,381 --> 00:09:04,448
I don't.

136
00:09:05,082 --> 00:09:06,884
It's not like I have things to talk about.

137
00:09:09,553 --> 00:09:10,788
-Good morning.
-Morning.

138
00:09:10,855 --> 00:09:12,690
-Good morning.
-Good morning, Ayano.

139
00:09:21,532 --> 00:09:22,600
What's wrong?

140
00:09:24,335 --> 00:09:27,238
I'm kind of jealous of you, Ayano.

141
00:09:27,905 --> 00:09:28,873
Look at me.

142
00:09:29,373 --> 00:09:31,676
My bangs are always messy.

143
00:09:33,177 --> 00:09:36,080
I want plumper under-eyes.

144
00:09:36,147 --> 00:09:39,183
Don't worry about it, Cocoa.
You're plenty cute as you are.

145
00:09:43,554 --> 00:09:46,691
It must be nice to be you.
You're always so composed.

146
00:09:47,358 --> 00:09:49,226
It's like you don't have any worries.

147
00:09:50,895 --> 00:09:54,231
No way. I'm dreading
cram school later today.

148
00:10:12,650 --> 00:10:14,185
RESIGNATION LETTER

149
00:10:16,587 --> 00:10:18,355
PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE

150
00:10:19,457 --> 00:10:20,458
Good morning.

151
00:10:20,524 --> 00:10:22,259
Good morning.

152
00:10:22,893 --> 00:10:23,994
Principal.

153
00:10:24,995 --> 00:10:26,997
What is it, Ms. Kashiwabara?

154
00:10:30,134 --> 00:10:32,403
Do you have a moment?

155
00:10:36,941 --> 00:10:39,143
I have something important to discuss.

156
00:10:39,210 --> 00:10:40,945
Oh? What is it?

157
00:10:41,011 --> 00:10:42,646
It's a bit hard to say…

158
00:10:45,349 --> 00:10:46,684
I…

159
00:10:50,588 --> 00:10:53,390
Please wait a moment.

160
00:10:53,457 --> 00:10:54,391
What is it?

161
00:10:54,458 --> 00:10:55,926
No, I…

162
00:10:57,061 --> 00:10:58,896
I have a wife!

163
00:10:58,963 --> 00:11:00,865
No! That's not it. I'm sorry.

164
00:11:00,931 --> 00:11:03,667
It's because of my contact lenses…
You have the wrong idea.

165
00:11:03,734 --> 00:11:05,202
Hey, what are you doing?

166
00:11:05,269 --> 00:11:07,204
-You walked right into us.
-Yeah.

167
00:11:07,271 --> 00:11:09,273
What? You guys bumped into me!

168
00:11:09,340 --> 00:11:12,409
We were just hanging out here.

169
00:11:12,977 --> 00:11:16,313
-You shouldn't be hanging out here!
-Why? This is a public space!

170
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:17,681
PROCEED TO MATCHING PLAN

171
00:11:17,748 --> 00:11:18,883
I'm sorry.

172
00:11:22,453 --> 00:11:25,322
Ms. Kashiwabara, what is it?

173
00:11:27,124 --> 00:11:28,759
That important thing you mentioned…

174
00:11:28,826 --> 00:11:29,860
What?

175
00:11:30,628 --> 00:11:32,830
Oh, I have to go!

176
00:11:35,466 --> 00:11:37,701
I'M COCOA

177
00:11:37,768 --> 00:11:41,105
LOOKING FOR A WONDERFUL MAN
TO GO TO KARAOKE WITH

178
00:11:51,882 --> 00:11:54,885
Let's pretend I didn't see that.
I'm quitting anyway.

179
00:12:02,092 --> 00:12:04,361
MR. ONIZUKA
ONE UNREAD MESSAGE

180
00:12:05,329 --> 00:12:07,131
FORGOT TO TELL YOU
SOMETHING IMPORTANT YESTERDAY

181
00:12:07,798 --> 00:12:09,133
What?

182
00:12:09,767 --> 00:12:12,102
PLEASE TAKE CARE OF OUR STUDENTS FOR ME

183
00:12:13,204 --> 00:12:14,972
Oh, jeez.

184
00:12:16,507 --> 00:12:18,142
Ms. Cocoa Ishibashi.

185
00:12:19,810 --> 00:12:20,778
What is it?

186
00:12:20,845 --> 00:12:24,481
If you're trying to do sugar dating,
you should stop.

187
00:12:26,217 --> 00:12:29,620
Why not? I just go to karaoke with them,
and they give me money.

188
00:12:29,687 --> 00:12:32,623
You say that, but what if you
get into a dangerous situation?

189
00:12:32,690 --> 00:12:36,293
Besides, if you get caught, you might get
expelled since you're a minor.

190
00:12:37,528 --> 00:12:39,129
Then please stay quiet about it.

191
00:12:39,630 --> 00:12:41,632
I really need money.

192
00:12:41,699 --> 00:12:42,700
Why?

193
00:12:44,869 --> 00:12:46,270
That's because…

194
00:12:49,673 --> 00:12:51,108
I'm getting plastic surgery.

195
00:12:51,709 --> 00:12:52,576
What?

196
00:12:52,643 --> 00:12:54,678
I can only earn money right now.

197
00:12:54,745 --> 00:12:57,882
If I'm not a high school girl,
no one will pick me.

198
00:12:57,948 --> 00:13:00,651
That's not true, Ms. Cocoa.
You are lovely as you are.

199
00:13:04,922 --> 00:13:06,223
You know…

200
00:13:06,290 --> 00:13:07,358
What?

201
00:13:07,424 --> 00:13:09,927
You sound so condescending.

202
00:13:10,494 --> 00:13:14,298
Miss, you're pretty and smart,
so I bet you can easily get what you want.

203
00:13:14,365 --> 00:13:16,634
-That's not true--
-Please.

204
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:18,569
Could you stop meddling in my life?

205
00:13:18,636 --> 00:13:20,671
You may be Onizuka's henchman…

206
00:13:20,738 --> 00:13:22,006
Wait a moment, I am not--

207
00:13:22,072 --> 00:13:23,607
Just leave me alone already!

208
00:13:24,408 --> 00:13:26,277
I won't cause trouble for you, Miss.

209
00:13:34,184 --> 00:13:35,085
Goodbye.

210
00:13:35,152 --> 00:13:36,320
Goodbye.

211
00:13:37,755 --> 00:13:39,957
Maybe I should try talking to him.

212
00:13:57,141 --> 00:13:58,575
What's wrong? What happened?

213
00:13:59,343 --> 00:14:02,012
I wanted to talk, just the two of us.

214
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:03,814
This is not good.

215
00:14:03,881 --> 00:14:05,616
-What?
-It's best we don't talk at school.

216
00:14:05,683 --> 00:14:07,751
Just a little is fine.

217
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:11,722
I'll contact you when school is over.

218
00:14:14,124 --> 00:14:15,059
Got it.

219
00:14:32,876 --> 00:14:35,879
Come on, give me a break…

220
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:39,683
SEISHIN HIGH SCHOOL

221
00:14:42,519 --> 00:14:43,487
What?

222
00:14:44,955 --> 00:14:47,458
-Don't come to my school…
-What?

223
00:14:47,524 --> 00:14:48,959
Are you talking to us?

224
00:14:51,261 --> 00:14:54,231
Mr. Soma Sato, what's wrong?

225
00:14:56,133 --> 00:14:57,634
Nothing.

226
00:15:02,539 --> 00:15:03,507
Who are those kids?

227
00:15:04,742 --> 00:15:05,843
They're acquaintances.

228
00:15:05,909 --> 00:15:07,077
What were you talking about?

229
00:15:08,879 --> 00:15:10,247
Just small talk.

230
00:15:15,419 --> 00:15:17,187
What is with everyone…

231
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:30,834
Hello, Mom?

232
00:15:31,835 --> 00:15:33,270
I'm going to cram school now.

233
00:15:35,472 --> 00:15:36,540
I know.

234
00:15:37,107 --> 00:15:38,008
Bye then.

235
00:15:43,814 --> 00:15:45,115
Do your best.

236
00:15:53,057 --> 00:15:54,291
Huh?

237
00:15:56,827 --> 00:15:57,828
No…

238
00:16:01,598 --> 00:16:03,333
I didn't see anything…

239
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,169
I didn't see anything…

240
00:16:08,038 --> 00:16:09,706
I'm exhausted.

241
00:16:12,042 --> 00:16:13,010
Hey, Chapu-Chapu.

242
00:16:13,077 --> 00:16:17,347
I'm about to quit, so why do I keep
witnessing things I don't wanna see?

243
00:16:17,915 --> 00:16:21,185
Maybe fate is telling you,
"Don't quit being a teacher."

244
00:16:21,251 --> 00:16:23,187
No, it's the other way around!

245
00:16:23,253 --> 00:16:26,890
God is telling me to quit being a teacher
because it's such a pain!

246
00:16:26,957 --> 00:16:30,928
Hey, if you're troubled, why don't you
consult someone you can trust?

247
00:16:31,895 --> 00:16:33,764
I have no one like that…

248
00:16:34,331 --> 00:16:35,165
Right.

249
00:16:35,232 --> 00:16:38,035
What do you think
Mr. Onizuka would do at a time like this?

250
00:16:38,102 --> 00:16:40,737
CONVERSING

251
00:16:41,472 --> 00:16:42,840
Are you listening, Chapu-Chapu?

252
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:45,242
Miyo, could it be…

253
00:16:45,309 --> 00:16:47,744
you like Mr. Onizuka?

254
00:16:47,811 --> 00:16:49,947
Wait, stop that.

255
00:16:50,013 --> 00:16:51,782
How old do you think he is?

256
00:16:51,849 --> 00:16:55,385
But lately, I feel like
you talk about him an awful lot.

257
00:16:55,452 --> 00:16:57,621
Why would I like that old man…

258
00:16:58,622 --> 00:17:01,758
Oh, enough already. I'll submit
my resignation tomorrow!

259
00:17:02,259 --> 00:17:06,230
Set the air conditioner to 26 degrees,
and brighten the lighting a little.

260
00:17:07,297 --> 00:17:08,632
500 watts for one minute.

261
00:17:08,699 --> 00:17:11,168
Oh, play some music to cheer me up!

262
00:17:19,143 --> 00:17:19,977
Principal!

263
00:17:21,812 --> 00:17:22,980
What is it?

264
00:17:25,382 --> 00:17:26,750
Actually, I…

265
00:17:26,817 --> 00:17:28,986
Hey, don't mess around! What the heck?

266
00:17:29,052 --> 00:17:30,420
-Oh?
-What?

267
00:17:30,487 --> 00:17:32,389
Isn't that your class?

268
00:17:33,790 --> 00:17:35,559
I have to go!

269
00:17:36,126 --> 00:17:38,695
Hey, you got a problem? Stop it.

270
00:17:38,762 --> 00:17:39,997
Oh, wow!

271
00:17:40,063 --> 00:17:41,331
Give it back!

272
00:17:41,398 --> 00:17:43,233
Are you doing sugar dating?

273
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:45,369
Still, isn't this face a bit much?

274
00:17:45,435 --> 00:17:48,071
You used too many filters.
It's like a different person!

275
00:17:48,138 --> 00:17:50,541
It has nothing to do with you guys!

276
00:17:50,607 --> 00:17:53,544
Hey, does this stuff pay a lot?
We should do it too.

277
00:17:53,610 --> 00:17:55,546
Hey, give it back!

278
00:17:55,612 --> 00:17:57,414
What are you doing?!

279
00:17:58,382 --> 00:18:00,350
No, we were just messing around.

280
00:18:01,285 --> 00:18:02,286
Right?

281
00:18:05,355 --> 00:18:06,590
Ms. Ishibashi!

282
00:18:12,362 --> 00:18:15,098
Jeez, give me a break already.

283
00:18:27,144 --> 00:18:29,813
MR. ONIZUKA

284
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:32,349
HOW ARE YOU FEELING?
GET BETTER QUICKLY AND COME BACK

285
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:38,555
SORRY, I CAME DOWN
WITH A BAD CASE OF DIARRHEA…

286
00:18:38,622 --> 00:18:40,257
What the heck?

287
00:18:40,324 --> 00:18:41,258
Ms. Kashiwabara.

288
00:18:41,325 --> 00:18:42,159
Yes?

289
00:18:42,226 --> 00:18:45,829
I heard a female student from your class
went home. What happened?

290
00:18:45,896 --> 00:18:47,664
Oh, she was sugar da--

291
00:18:47,731 --> 00:18:48,632
"Da" what?

292
00:18:49,466 --> 00:18:50,300
Da…

293
00:18:50,367 --> 00:18:52,836
She dashed home so fast,
I didn't find out anything yet!

294
00:18:52,903 --> 00:18:57,307
Go talk to her, and fast. You are
in charge of Class 1-B, after all.

295
00:19:00,077 --> 00:19:01,011
But I…

296
00:19:01,078 --> 00:19:01,979
What is it?

297
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:05,182
RESIGNATION LETTER

298
00:19:06,450 --> 00:19:09,786
Vice Principal, I have
a very important matter to…

299
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:11,088
What?

300
00:19:11,822 --> 00:19:14,024
It's hard to say… Actually…

301
00:19:14,958 --> 00:19:16,026
Oh, no.

302
00:19:16,994 --> 00:19:20,797
My wife only left me recently, but…

303
00:19:21,865 --> 00:19:24,501
If that's how you feel, Miss…

304
00:19:24,568 --> 00:19:25,435
What?

305
00:19:26,303 --> 00:19:28,138
No!

306
00:19:29,172 --> 00:19:31,675
Why does everyone misunderstand me?

307
00:19:35,212 --> 00:19:36,346
Please, come in.

308
00:19:36,413 --> 00:19:37,447
Excuse me.

309
00:19:37,514 --> 00:19:39,516
This is my husband and son.

310
00:19:39,583 --> 00:19:41,218
Sorry to interrupt your meal.

311
00:19:41,285 --> 00:19:44,388
It's fine. We're sorry our daughter
caused you trouble.

312
00:19:45,555 --> 00:19:46,990
Where is Ms. Cocoa?

313
00:19:47,057 --> 00:19:50,093
Since she came home,
she hasn't come out of her room.

314
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:52,362
She said she won't go to school anymore.

315
00:19:52,429 --> 00:19:54,498
Just leave her be. She'll come out.

316
00:19:54,564 --> 00:19:56,266
She has always been like this.

317
00:19:56,333 --> 00:20:00,570
Since she was young, when there's
something she doesn't like, she sulks.

318
00:20:01,138 --> 00:20:02,139
Really?

319
00:20:02,205 --> 00:20:04,241
Remember that time back in middle school?

320
00:20:04,308 --> 00:20:06,943
Yeah. She wanted a new smartphone…

321
00:20:07,511 --> 00:20:09,179
COCOA

322
00:20:09,246 --> 00:20:12,649
Cocoa? Your homeroom teacher is here.

323
00:20:16,153 --> 00:20:18,789
Ms. Cocoa, do you have a moment?

324
00:20:20,924 --> 00:20:22,559
I'm coming in.

325
00:20:35,138 --> 00:20:36,840
What a cute room.

326
00:20:38,508 --> 00:20:42,412
No matter what you say,
I'm not going to school anymore.

327
00:20:42,479 --> 00:20:45,982
Don't say things like that.
Your parents were worried too.

328
00:20:48,218 --> 00:20:49,753
Nothing but lies.

329
00:20:49,820 --> 00:20:53,523
Those people could never
understand my feelings.

330
00:20:53,590 --> 00:20:54,524
Why?

331
00:20:55,092 --> 00:20:57,527
Because they have
confidence in themselves,

332
00:20:57,594 --> 00:21:00,397
so they don't understand
how important looks are these days.

333
00:21:01,264 --> 00:21:04,768
If only they had given birth to me
with looks like Kotone or Ayano,

334
00:21:04,835 --> 00:21:06,937
I wouldn't have had to worry like this.

335
00:21:08,438 --> 00:21:11,908
I already told you,
you don't need to worry at all.

336
00:21:11,975 --> 00:21:13,276
Did you know?

337
00:21:13,343 --> 00:21:16,580
80 percent of Japanese people
have a gene called

338
00:21:16,646 --> 00:21:20,183
the serotonin transporter that makes us
feel anxious easily, apparently.

339
00:21:20,250 --> 00:21:22,819
So it's best you don't worry
unnecessarily…

340
00:21:24,054 --> 00:21:27,457
You keep going on and on,
acting all high and mighty…

341
00:21:27,524 --> 00:21:28,458
What?

342
00:21:28,525 --> 00:21:30,627
What you are doing right now

343
00:21:30,694 --> 00:21:33,764
is just harassing me with your logic,
emotions, and authority!

344
00:21:34,331 --> 00:21:35,399
What are you saying?

345
00:21:35,465 --> 00:21:39,169
Except for this dog,
no one cares about me at all.

346
00:21:39,236 --> 00:21:41,805
That's why my family is still so carefree,

347
00:21:41,872 --> 00:21:44,708
and not a single one
of my classmates has contacted me.

348
00:21:53,316 --> 00:21:54,217
Who is it?

349
00:21:56,253 --> 00:21:57,220
Onizuka.

350
00:21:57,287 --> 00:21:59,156
COCOA, YOU OKAY?
SORRY I COULDN'T VISIT YOU

351
00:21:59,222 --> 00:22:01,691
See? He's worried about you.

352
00:22:02,426 --> 00:22:05,695
That's just because it's his job.
Same goes for you, doesn't it?

353
00:22:06,263 --> 00:22:08,098
No, well…

354
00:22:08,165 --> 00:22:10,801
Man, I wish I could be reincarnated.

355
00:22:10,867 --> 00:22:13,670
Being a high school girl
in this day and age is too hard.

356
00:22:13,737 --> 00:22:16,506
It feels like you're tied
to social media 24/7.

357
00:22:16,573 --> 00:22:18,909
If someone DMs you asking,
"Are you watching this show?"

358
00:22:18,975 --> 00:22:22,345
even if you don't care, you have to reply,
or they'll think you're ignoring them.

359
00:22:22,412 --> 00:22:24,347
And when talking with classmates,

360
00:22:24,414 --> 00:22:28,685
all I'm doing is agreeing
with them all day long.

361
00:22:29,252 --> 00:22:30,320
You know,

362
00:22:30,887 --> 00:22:34,157
watching influencers who have it all
figured out on social media,

363
00:22:34,224 --> 00:22:38,428
I feel like I'll never stand
on the same stage as them.

364
00:22:38,495 --> 00:22:40,931
So all I feel is sheer despair.

365
00:22:42,132 --> 00:22:46,069
I wish I was at least
born into a rich family.

366
00:22:46,136 --> 00:22:48,405
I could spend
my inheritance living in a hotel

367
00:22:48,472 --> 00:22:50,106
and enjoy life forever.

368
00:22:50,173 --> 00:22:51,942
Right, Pudding?

369
00:22:53,243 --> 00:22:56,947
You keep babbling on and on
about boring nonsense…

370
00:22:57,747 --> 00:22:58,682
What?

371
00:22:59,249 --> 00:23:01,351
When you get down to it,
all you're saying is

372
00:23:01,418 --> 00:23:04,387
you don't want to get hurt,
you don't want to do anything yourself,

373
00:23:04,454 --> 00:23:08,825
but you want what others have, and you
don't want to be made fun of or ignored.

374
00:23:08,892 --> 00:23:10,894
What I hate most about being a teacher

375
00:23:10,961 --> 00:23:15,398
is having to deal with brats like you who
have absurdly high pride and nothing else.

376
00:23:15,465 --> 00:23:20,036
Sorry, but I don't have time to cater to
your pathetic need for validation anymore.

377
00:23:21,304 --> 00:23:23,840
You don't have to say it so harshly.

378
00:23:23,907 --> 00:23:27,677
You cry right away whenever someone
says something rough… Do what you want!

379
00:23:27,744 --> 00:23:31,181
If you don't want to come to school,
don't! I'm quitting teaching anyway.

380
00:23:32,649 --> 00:23:33,483
What?

381
00:23:43,460 --> 00:23:45,328
I messed up big time.

382
00:23:48,565 --> 00:23:49,633
Good morning.

383
00:23:49,699 --> 00:23:50,534
Morning.

384
00:23:50,600 --> 00:23:52,502
Good morning.

385
00:23:53,069 --> 00:23:54,671
Good morning.

386
00:24:02,646 --> 00:24:04,147
ABOUT YOUR REPLY TO OUR OFFER

387
00:24:04,214 --> 00:24:06,216
COULD WE GET A REPLY ABOUT OUR OFFER?

388
00:24:11,588 --> 00:24:14,791
SORRY FOR MY LATE REPLY.
I GLADLY ACCEPT YOUR OFFER.

389
00:24:20,230 --> 00:24:21,498
KASHIWABARA

390
00:24:21,565 --> 00:24:22,832
Ms. Kashiwabara.

391
00:24:22,899 --> 00:24:24,634
Yes? What is it?

392
00:24:24,701 --> 00:24:28,038
I know it must be rough
not having Mr. Onizuka around,

393
00:24:28,104 --> 00:24:30,040
but please take good care of Class 1-B.

394
00:24:30,674 --> 00:24:31,508
What?

395
00:24:31,575 --> 00:24:34,544
Mr. Onizuka even said
he really relies on you.

396
00:24:34,611 --> 00:24:37,080
No, but I…

397
00:24:37,147 --> 00:24:37,981
What?

398
00:24:38,882 --> 00:24:40,417
I mean, I…

399
00:24:42,385 --> 00:24:45,021
This is not good.
It's best we don't talk at school.

400
00:24:45,088 --> 00:24:46,056
It's fine.

401
00:24:47,490 --> 00:24:48,758
Mr. Miyazawa…

402
00:24:48,825 --> 00:24:50,026
Well…

403
00:24:50,894 --> 00:24:51,828
Yes?

404
00:24:52,696 --> 00:24:54,264
Are you dating someone?

405
00:24:55,198 --> 00:24:56,800
What? Um… I…

406
00:24:56,866 --> 00:24:58,501
Please don't misunderstand!

407
00:24:58,568 --> 00:25:01,104
It's not like I have
feelings for you or anything.

408
00:25:01,705 --> 00:25:03,006
Then why ask?

409
00:25:03,807 --> 00:25:04,874
Because…

410
00:25:07,010 --> 00:25:08,645
Never mind.

411
00:25:09,479 --> 00:25:10,947
Excuse me.

412
00:25:13,249 --> 00:25:14,084
CLASS 1-B

413
00:25:14,150 --> 00:25:16,753
"'What sort of frame is it?'
Her Highness asked him.

414
00:25:16,820 --> 00:25:18,622
'It is altogether magnificent,'
he replied."

415
00:25:18,688 --> 00:25:22,459
People say, 'It is a frame design unlike
anything they have ever seen before.'

416
00:25:22,525 --> 00:25:26,229
'Indeed, I myself have never seen
anything like it,' he stated proudly.

417
00:25:26,296 --> 00:25:29,666
Then, I remarked, 'Well then, that must
be the frame, or bones, of a jellyfish.'

418
00:25:29,733 --> 00:25:33,370
'I’ll claim that joke as my own!'
Takaie replied, and laughed heartily.

419
00:25:34,170 --> 00:25:37,907
Things like this are usually included
among laughable matters,

420
00:25:37,974 --> 00:25:39,776
but as a small story…"

421
00:25:39,843 --> 00:25:42,479
My daughter left for school earlier today.

422
00:25:42,545 --> 00:25:44,214
Oh, really?

423
00:25:44,914 --> 00:25:47,183
What? She didn't go?

424
00:25:48,084 --> 00:25:52,155
Did Ms. Cocoa say anything about me?

425
00:25:52,222 --> 00:25:53,323
Since that night.

426
00:25:54,057 --> 00:25:55,325
No, not really.

427
00:25:55,392 --> 00:25:59,496
She ate and slept normally,
so I was even a little relieved.

428
00:26:02,132 --> 00:26:03,266
I understand.

429
00:26:03,333 --> 00:26:06,002
I'll try calling her from my end.

430
00:26:06,069 --> 00:26:07,671
Excuse me.

431
00:26:12,509 --> 00:26:16,246
The person you are calling
cannot come to the phone right now…

432
00:26:16,312 --> 00:26:17,814
Ms. Kashiwabara.

433
00:26:17,881 --> 00:26:19,115
Yes?

434
00:26:20,016 --> 00:26:21,651
You said you had…

435
00:26:22,652 --> 00:26:24,454
something important to tell me.

436
00:26:25,188 --> 00:26:26,389
Right.

437
00:26:26,456 --> 00:26:27,691
What is it?

438
00:26:29,492 --> 00:26:31,027
Well, actually…

439
00:26:34,564 --> 00:26:35,331
RESIGNATION LETTER

440
00:26:39,102 --> 00:26:40,403
You can't quit.

441
00:26:40,470 --> 00:26:43,306
Out of everyone I know,
you're the most suited to being a teacher.

442
00:26:43,373 --> 00:26:46,609
Mr. Onizuka even said
he really relies on you.

443
00:26:47,711 --> 00:26:48,611
Oh, come on!

444
00:26:48,678 --> 00:26:50,246
I have to go!

445
00:26:51,715 --> 00:26:54,184
SEISHIN HIGH SCHOOL

446
00:27:11,034 --> 00:27:12,302
Ms. Cocoa.

447
00:27:15,271 --> 00:27:17,006
Sorry for making you wait.

448
00:27:17,073 --> 00:27:18,208
It's okay.

449
00:27:18,274 --> 00:27:19,476
-Let's go.
-Yeah.

450
00:27:32,322 --> 00:27:34,858
MS. COCOA, ARE YOU OKAY?
DON'T DO ANYTHING RECKLESS

451
00:27:38,261 --> 00:27:40,597
MS. COCOA, ARE YOU OKAY?
DON'T DO ANYTHING RECKLESS

452
00:27:45,802 --> 00:27:48,004
LEAVE ME ALONE

453
00:27:52,809 --> 00:27:55,278
What am I even doing?

454
00:28:04,154 --> 00:28:06,089
I'M ALMOST THERE

455
00:28:13,163 --> 00:28:16,933
IF I GO WITH YOU TO A HOTEL
WILL YOU GIVE ME 30,000 YEN?

456
00:28:27,844 --> 00:28:29,946
GOT IT

457
00:28:40,156 --> 00:28:41,791
What do you want for dinner?

458
00:28:47,897 --> 00:28:51,935
I'll count down, and if Onizuka
texts me before I reach zero,

459
00:28:52,836 --> 00:28:54,103
I'll go home.

460
00:28:56,639 --> 00:28:57,774
Ten.

461
00:28:58,842 --> 00:28:59,776
Nine.

462
00:29:01,411 --> 00:29:02,445
Eight.

463
00:29:03,847 --> 00:29:04,781
Seven.

464
00:29:05,882 --> 00:29:06,783
Six.

465
00:29:08,084 --> 00:29:08,918
Five.

466
00:29:10,286 --> 00:29:11,387
Four.

467
00:29:12,488 --> 00:29:13,656
Three.

468
00:29:14,724 --> 00:29:15,658
Two.

469
00:29:17,393 --> 00:29:18,361
One.

470
00:29:19,395 --> 00:29:20,463
Zero.

471
00:29:33,610 --> 00:29:35,144
Sorry for making you wait!

472
00:29:35,712 --> 00:29:37,213
Why are you here?

473
00:29:37,280 --> 00:29:39,482
We made plans, didn't we?

474
00:29:39,549 --> 00:29:41,584
MEET AT 5 P.M.

475
00:29:42,552 --> 00:29:43,419
No way.

476
00:29:43,486 --> 00:29:44,387
Well,

477
00:29:45,188 --> 00:29:47,757
shall we go? You'll come
with me to a hotel, right?

478
00:29:50,193 --> 00:29:53,196
What, are you scared?

479
00:29:55,031 --> 00:29:56,266
No way.

480
00:30:08,611 --> 00:30:09,612
-Hey.
-What?

481
00:30:09,679 --> 00:30:11,314
Are you really giving me money?

482
00:30:11,381 --> 00:30:14,884
Of course. Let's see, 30,000…

483
00:30:14,951 --> 00:30:16,386
Cut it out, not here.

484
00:30:16,452 --> 00:30:17,453
Oh, sorry.

485
00:30:18,021 --> 00:30:21,291
But is this okay? You're a teacher.
They'll fire you, you know.

486
00:30:21,357 --> 00:30:24,661
What, are you worried about me?
Should we go back then?

487
00:30:25,862 --> 00:30:27,330
Of course not.

488
00:30:35,605 --> 00:30:37,740
Hey, are you running away?

489
00:30:41,511 --> 00:30:43,880
Excuse me, are you okay?

490
00:30:43,947 --> 00:30:45,214
I'll move you, okay?

491
00:30:47,283 --> 00:30:48,184
What do we do?

492
00:30:48,251 --> 00:30:50,053
What are you doing? Call an ambulance!

493
00:30:50,119 --> 00:30:51,354
Got it!

494
00:30:52,021 --> 00:30:53,589
And bring an AED!

495
00:30:53,656 --> 00:30:54,891
Got it!

496
00:30:54,958 --> 00:30:57,493
What, an AED?

497
00:30:58,061 --> 00:30:58,795
Hurry!

498
00:31:23,653 --> 00:31:25,822
Chapu-Chapu, I've made up my mind.

499
00:31:25,888 --> 00:31:28,358
I'm definitely quitting this teacher job.

500
00:31:28,424 --> 00:31:30,727
CONVERSING

501
00:31:32,462 --> 00:31:34,797
Chapu-Chapu, aren't you going
to say anything?

502
00:31:34,864 --> 00:31:36,833
CONVERSING

503
00:31:49,178 --> 00:31:51,681
Hello. Sorry for calling so late at night.

504
00:31:51,748 --> 00:31:55,885
My name is Kashiwabara.
I'm calling about your offer…

505
00:31:56,853 --> 00:31:59,922
Oh, please excuse me.

506
00:32:03,960 --> 00:32:05,595
What, why?

507
00:32:05,661 --> 00:32:08,364
Well, a lot happened.

508
00:32:08,431 --> 00:32:12,068
But Cocoa was amazing.

509
00:32:12,802 --> 00:32:13,736
What?

510
00:32:16,406 --> 00:32:19,509
We found a woman unconscious,

511
00:32:19,575 --> 00:32:22,779
but thanks to Cocoa performing CPR,

512
00:32:22,845 --> 00:32:24,747
her life was saved.

513
00:32:25,681 --> 00:32:27,917
My grandma has heart issues,

514
00:32:28,751 --> 00:32:30,686
and she had an attack.

515
00:32:32,088 --> 00:32:35,458
I couldn't do anything back then,
and it frustrated me,

516
00:32:36,159 --> 00:32:37,126
so I studied a lot.

517
00:32:38,494 --> 00:32:39,529
I see.

518
00:32:40,797 --> 00:32:44,167
Besides, anyone could do
something like that.

519
00:32:44,934 --> 00:32:48,438
No, I think only you could have done that.

520
00:32:49,172 --> 00:32:50,039
What?

521
00:32:51,641 --> 00:32:53,276
When I saw you

522
00:32:54,077 --> 00:32:57,213
desperately doing chest compressions,

523
00:32:57,280 --> 00:33:00,049
single-mindedly
wishing for her to be okay…

524
00:33:00,950 --> 00:33:02,518
It made me think…

525
00:33:03,386 --> 00:33:07,490
"What I am looking at is true beauty."

526
00:33:10,927 --> 00:33:14,497
That was, you know, how should I put it?

527
00:33:14,564 --> 00:33:17,633
Something only you have…

528
00:33:19,235 --> 00:33:22,605
Ms. Kashiwabara!
Say something impressive as usual.

529
00:33:24,307 --> 00:33:24,974
What?

530
00:33:28,945 --> 00:33:30,279
I…

531
00:33:34,283 --> 00:33:35,718
Give me a break!

532
00:33:36,285 --> 00:33:38,488
I've already decided
to quit being a teacher!

533
00:33:39,522 --> 00:33:41,324
There you go with that again…

534
00:33:41,390 --> 00:33:44,460
I'm just sick of it!
Such a hassle of a job!

535
00:33:44,527 --> 00:33:47,363
I can't do this, can't do that,
because of "compliance"…

536
00:33:47,430 --> 00:33:49,799
Always walking on eggshells
around sassy brats…

537
00:33:49,866 --> 00:33:52,869
And when they go overboard and I warn
them, I get accused of harassment.

538
00:33:53,603 --> 00:33:55,371
When I scold them for their own good

539
00:33:55,438 --> 00:33:58,508
and they give an exaggerated sigh,
it pisses me off.

540
00:33:59,542 --> 00:34:00,443
And besides,

541
00:34:00,510 --> 00:34:03,513
after-school activities, dealing with
parents, it's too much unpaid overtime.

542
00:34:03,579 --> 00:34:06,716
It's like none of this "work reform"
reached us teachers at all!

543
00:34:06,782 --> 00:34:07,984
No, but,

544
00:34:08,751 --> 00:34:11,621
isn't it fun being with the kids in class?

545
00:34:11,687 --> 00:34:14,457
That side of you pisses me off too!

546
00:34:14,524 --> 00:34:18,194
Irresponsible, oblivious, and a total
nuisance, yet you still enjoy yourself!

547
00:34:19,962 --> 00:34:21,097
It's not like I…

548
00:34:21,164 --> 00:34:24,233
Must be nice to act without
thinking of the consequences,

549
00:34:24,300 --> 00:34:26,335
but I can't do that!

550
00:34:26,402 --> 00:34:30,239
I don't even actually like kids!
I don't like dealing with people either!

551
00:34:30,306 --> 00:34:33,409
I find it annoying to take calls
from my parents in the countryside!

552
00:34:33,476 --> 00:34:35,378
Talking to AI is when I feel
the most at ease!

553
00:34:35,444 --> 00:34:38,948
Do I really have to keep being a teacher?

554
00:34:39,882 --> 00:34:40,750
Of course you do!

555
00:34:40,816 --> 00:34:42,351
Why do I?

556
00:34:46,689 --> 00:34:48,124
Because there are many things

557
00:34:49,792 --> 00:34:52,962
only you can teach!

558
00:34:54,530 --> 00:34:55,598
What?

559
00:34:55,665 --> 00:34:56,999
With the knowledge

560
00:34:58,134 --> 00:35:00,069
and words that only you can convey,

561
00:35:01,003 --> 00:35:04,707
you have saved so many kids in our class.

562
00:35:05,942 --> 00:35:07,109
You're always cool-headed,

563
00:35:08,277 --> 00:35:11,113
and you observe the students properly,

564
00:35:11,180 --> 00:35:13,416
so you notice tiny changes
before anyone else.

565
00:35:14,183 --> 00:35:16,752
Who else is more suited
to be a teacher than that?

566
00:35:17,653 --> 00:35:22,024
Plus, you have
way more time left than I do!

567
00:35:22,625 --> 00:35:25,528
From my perspective, it's like,
"Don't mess with me, damn it!"

568
00:35:26,229 --> 00:35:28,497
If you're going to quit,
give that time to me!

569
00:35:29,131 --> 00:35:31,067
You don't realize how fortunate you are,

570
00:35:31,133 --> 00:35:33,536
yet you keep imposing
restrictions on yourself…

571
00:35:34,270 --> 00:35:36,339
Maybe you shouldn't push yourself…

572
00:35:36,872 --> 00:35:39,642
No, I need to lecture her more.

573
00:35:41,644 --> 00:35:42,745
Also,

574
00:35:44,146 --> 00:35:46,582
can you stop badmouthing being a teacher?

575
00:35:47,516 --> 00:35:51,654
Every day, you get
to witness children grow!

576
00:35:51,721 --> 00:35:54,757
Is there any other job
as wonderful as this?

577
00:35:58,194 --> 00:35:59,495
Wait, are you okay?

578
00:36:00,496 --> 00:36:02,898
Aren't you pushing yourself
too hard? You okay?

579
00:36:18,481 --> 00:36:19,482
What?

580
00:36:21,751 --> 00:36:23,786
-Are you awake?
-Yeah.

581
00:36:23,853 --> 00:36:25,588
Here, take your temperature.

582
00:36:27,056 --> 00:36:29,058
Huh? Where's Cocoa?

583
00:36:29,125 --> 00:36:30,760
She went home yesterday.

584
00:36:31,327 --> 00:36:34,096
She laughed and said,
"Mr. Onizuka has a cold,

585
00:36:34,163 --> 00:36:36,966
yet he pushed himself so hard.
He's such an idiot!"

586
00:36:37,033 --> 00:36:38,634
My bad.

587
00:36:39,835 --> 00:36:41,537
Let me see.

588
00:36:44,173 --> 00:36:45,541
It went down.

589
00:36:45,608 --> 00:36:48,344
I made some porridge,
so please eat if you'd like.

590
00:36:48,411 --> 00:36:49,745
Thank you.

591
00:36:50,546 --> 00:36:51,580
Oh, right.

592
00:36:52,481 --> 00:36:54,884
-I've been wondering for a while.
-Yeah?

593
00:36:54,950 --> 00:36:56,819
When you took time off,

594
00:36:56,886 --> 00:36:59,588
you threatened me,
saying you'd reveal my secret.

595
00:36:59,655 --> 00:37:00,956
So what is it?

596
00:37:02,692 --> 00:37:03,659
Right…

597
00:37:04,727 --> 00:37:06,562
That was, of course…

598
00:37:10,099 --> 00:37:14,503
That you, Ms. Kashiwabara,
are a better teacher than anyone else.

599
00:37:16,739 --> 00:37:18,174
What? Is that it?

600
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:19,108
I mean…

601
00:37:19,642 --> 00:37:22,678
Because some students
haven't realized it yet.

602
00:37:22,745 --> 00:37:24,980
So don't quit…

603
00:37:25,047 --> 00:37:28,484
Leave the key in the mailbox
when you leave. I'm heading to work.

604
00:37:28,551 --> 00:37:29,618
Wait, which job?

605
00:37:31,420 --> 00:37:33,589
Isn't it obvious?

606
00:37:37,126 --> 00:37:39,195
I am truly very sorry.

607
00:37:39,261 --> 00:37:42,298
I've decided I want to continue
with my current job after all.

608
00:37:42,365 --> 00:37:43,766
Excuse me.

609
00:37:50,406 --> 00:37:51,607
What's wrong?

610
00:37:51,674 --> 00:37:52,775
Ms. Cocoa.

611
00:37:54,844 --> 00:37:55,978
I just…

612
00:37:56,612 --> 00:38:00,116
couldn't build up the courage
to face everyone in class.

613
00:38:03,252 --> 00:38:04,520
You already have

614
00:38:05,488 --> 00:38:08,557
more than enough courage.

615
00:38:10,526 --> 00:38:11,360
What?

616
00:38:11,994 --> 00:38:13,796
When you saved someone yesterday,

617
00:38:14,397 --> 00:38:16,432
you had no hesitation.
Give yourself credit.

618
00:38:18,434 --> 00:38:22,071
Having courage means being strong.

619
00:38:23,239 --> 00:38:24,940
It means being kind.

620
00:38:26,242 --> 00:38:28,711
It means harboring incredible potential.

621
00:38:29,779 --> 00:38:30,713
So,

622
00:38:31,213 --> 00:38:34,984
from now on, I want you to be more aware
of the courage you possess

623
00:38:36,719 --> 00:38:38,354
and live with confidence.

624
00:38:43,125 --> 00:38:46,462
Then, maybe I'll be brave and say this.

625
00:38:46,529 --> 00:38:48,397
What? Say what?

626
00:38:50,966 --> 00:38:55,571
Up until now, I thought
growing up and getting a job

627
00:38:55,638 --> 00:38:57,873
sounded awful.

628
00:38:59,909 --> 00:39:04,046
But yesterday, after seeing you two argue,

629
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:08,451
I decided to stop thinking like that.

630
00:39:09,185 --> 00:39:10,286
Why?

631
00:39:11,587 --> 00:39:12,721
Because

632
00:39:14,657 --> 00:39:16,592
you made me want to become a teacher.

633
00:39:17,860 --> 00:39:18,727
What?

634
00:39:19,762 --> 00:39:22,898
So, I'll go with TC for my nickname.

635
00:39:23,933 --> 00:39:25,301
TC?

636
00:39:26,168 --> 00:39:27,937
Short for Teacher Cocoa.

637
00:39:31,907 --> 00:39:32,908
Got it.

638
00:39:33,576 --> 00:39:34,477
TC.

639
00:39:40,783 --> 00:39:41,917
Someday,

640
00:39:42,952 --> 00:39:46,922
I hope I can teach
at the same school as you, Miss.

641
00:40:08,410 --> 00:40:09,845
Good morning!

642
00:40:09,912 --> 00:40:11,347
Good morning.

643
00:40:11,413 --> 00:40:12,615
Good morning.

644
00:40:16,752 --> 00:40:17,786
All right.

645
00:40:17,853 --> 00:40:18,888
Ms. Kashiwabara.

646
00:40:18,954 --> 00:40:20,022
Yes?

647
00:40:20,089 --> 00:40:22,491
Looks like you resolved
your issue. That's great.

648
00:40:23,058 --> 00:40:24,627
Thank you very much.

649
00:40:25,628 --> 00:40:26,328
But…

650
00:40:27,263 --> 00:40:28,163
What?

651
00:40:28,864 --> 00:40:31,567
I don't know what I should say about you…

652
00:40:33,602 --> 00:40:35,938
Good morning!

653
00:40:36,005 --> 00:40:37,439
Good morning!

654
00:40:37,506 --> 00:40:38,507
Morning!

655
00:40:39,475 --> 00:40:43,279
Eikichi Onizuka
has fully recovered and returned!

656
00:40:43,345 --> 00:40:46,315
Why don't you take
the rest of the year off?

657
00:40:46,382 --> 00:40:48,484
There you go again.

658
00:40:48,551 --> 00:40:50,853
Bet you were lonely without me.

659
00:40:50,920 --> 00:40:52,621
-Shut up, go over there!
-Come on…

660
00:40:52,688 --> 00:40:53,822
Go away!

661
00:40:53,889 --> 00:40:58,894
It feels so refreshing
and nice in this staff room.

662
00:40:59,528 --> 00:41:01,597
Welcome back, Mr. Onizuka.

663
00:41:01,664 --> 00:41:03,666
Glad to see you feeling better.

664
00:41:04,233 --> 00:41:06,168
Mr. Murayama, Ms. Koizumi.

665
00:41:06,235 --> 00:41:08,571
I'll put even more effort into my work.

666
00:41:08,637 --> 00:41:10,773
So look forward to it. You too, Abechan.

667
00:41:10,839 --> 00:41:12,875
I told you to stop calling me that.

668
00:41:18,814 --> 00:41:19,982
Ms. Kashiwabara,

669
00:41:21,383 --> 00:41:22,585
I'm so glad.

670
00:41:23,953 --> 00:41:27,189
We'll be working together a while longer.

671
00:41:33,963 --> 00:41:36,899
Sorry for making you all worry.

672
00:41:37,466 --> 00:41:40,703
I, Eikichi Onizuka, am back.

673
00:41:42,037 --> 00:41:44,673
Let's make today a good day too.

674
00:41:46,475 --> 00:41:47,343
What?

675
00:41:47,910 --> 00:41:49,945
What's wrong? Hey.

676
00:41:50,012 --> 00:41:54,450
I thought you'd be like,
"Welcome back" or "Glad you're better."

677
00:41:59,088 --> 00:42:00,022
What happened?

678
00:42:00,089 --> 00:42:02,791
Your rating on the feedback system…

679
00:42:03,359 --> 00:42:05,127
Did it go up even more?

680
00:42:06,829 --> 00:42:08,497
Hey! What on earth is this?

681
00:42:08,564 --> 00:42:09,898
ONE GOOD RATING

682
00:42:09,965 --> 00:42:13,302
There's only one good rating left…

683
00:42:13,369 --> 00:42:15,537
By the way, that one's mine.

684
00:42:16,972 --> 00:42:20,609
Thank you. So, what about the rest of you?

685
00:42:20,676 --> 00:42:22,277
Yes, did something happen?

686
00:42:22,344 --> 00:42:23,545
It's a punishment.

687
00:42:23,612 --> 00:42:24,813
Punishment?

688
00:42:24,880 --> 00:42:28,450
Onicchi, you lied and said
you have a serious illness!

689
00:42:28,517 --> 00:42:30,319
We were genuinely worried…

690
00:42:30,386 --> 00:42:32,354
We feel like idiots.

691
00:42:32,421 --> 00:42:34,723
You can be too childish sometimes.

692
00:42:34,790 --> 00:42:38,861
You need to act a bit more like an adult.

693
00:42:38,927 --> 00:42:41,230
You've been awfully cocky lately.

694
00:42:41,296 --> 00:42:43,265
We need to punish you a bit.

695
00:42:43,332 --> 00:42:47,870
Oh, man, I'm sorry! I won't do it again!

696
00:42:47,936 --> 00:42:51,507
Keep on enjoying your youth!

697
00:42:52,241 --> 00:42:54,109
What should we do?

698
00:42:54,176 --> 00:42:57,312
If you tell us the test questions,
we might consider it.

699
00:42:57,379 --> 00:42:58,647
Leave it to me!

700
00:42:58,714 --> 00:43:00,449
What are you saying? Obviously not.

701
00:43:00,516 --> 00:43:01,350
Sorry…

702
00:43:01,417 --> 00:43:04,553
Why don't you all forgive him?
Mr. Onizuka seems to regret it.

703
00:43:06,288 --> 00:43:08,257
What should we do?

704
00:43:08,323 --> 00:43:11,026
I guess if Ms. Kashiwabara says so.

705
00:43:21,537 --> 00:43:23,806
EIKICHI ONIZUKA CLASS 1-B

706
00:43:23,872 --> 00:43:25,441
GOOD RATINGS

707
00:43:25,507 --> 00:43:28,944
I finally reached 25 good ratings!

708
00:43:30,045 --> 00:43:33,549
And all of you are looking up
from your tablets at me.

709
00:43:36,051 --> 00:43:38,921
At first, not a single one of you did…

710
00:43:53,168 --> 00:43:54,970
Is something wrong, Ms. Kashiwabara?

711
00:43:55,037 --> 00:43:56,038
No, nothing really.

712
00:43:57,406 --> 00:44:02,044
I still have three bad ratings left.

713
00:44:02,111 --> 00:44:04,747
It's like, "Who the heck are they?"

714
00:44:04,813 --> 00:44:06,915
You can't ask that. It's anonymous.

715
00:44:06,982 --> 00:44:08,183
Yeah, I know.

716
00:44:08,250 --> 00:44:13,789
All right, time for the second term's
schedule and things to keep in mind…

717
00:44:19,495 --> 00:44:22,030
HOW ABOUT YOU ALL STOP?
HOW STUPID CAN YOU BE?

718
00:44:22,097 --> 00:44:23,665
WHEN WILL YOU REALIZE HE'S TRICKING YOU?

719
00:44:23,732 --> 00:44:25,000
Wait, what is this?

720
00:44:25,701 --> 00:44:26,835
What?

721
00:44:28,170 --> 00:44:29,972
HE'S BEEN FIRED
FROM ALL HIS PREVIOUS SCHOOLS

722
00:44:30,038 --> 00:44:32,908
FOR USING VIOLENCE,
SEXUAL HARASSMENT, ETC.

723
00:44:32,975 --> 00:44:35,444
NO MATTER WHAT, I WON'T ACCEPT HIM

724
00:44:36,979 --> 00:44:38,647
I WON'T TRUST HIM,
EVEN IF I'M THE ONLY ONE LEFT

725
00:44:38,714 --> 00:44:39,748
Hey.

726
00:44:41,016 --> 00:44:44,219
Who the heck is still doing this?

727
00:44:50,759 --> 00:44:51,927
I am.

728
00:44:58,066 --> 00:45:00,803
How long are you going to let him
fool you? Are you stupid?

729
00:45:00,869 --> 00:45:02,805
Don't fight in class!

730
00:45:02,871 --> 00:45:05,574
Why do I have to keep
going through all this?

731
00:45:05,641 --> 00:45:06,441
Just leave me alone!

732
00:45:08,076 --> 00:45:11,580
Are former bike gang members
not allowed to become teachers?

733
00:45:11,647 --> 00:45:15,317
You sound a bit like Onizuka,
Ms. Kashiwabara.

734
00:45:15,384 --> 00:45:17,586
Who the hell rides something this uncool?

735
00:45:17,653 --> 00:45:18,987
You bastard!

736
00:45:19,054 --> 00:45:21,657
Both of you are lecturing me,
so high and mighty.

737
00:45:21,723 --> 00:45:23,025
It's over!

738
00:45:23,592 --> 00:45:26,028
Become smarter, Ayano.

739
00:45:26,094 --> 00:45:27,062
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

